{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787169895,"nonce":"dpQY7Xp135tqeNQU+iF+ACzWHNI=","message":"**One of the five observations on this ticket is now permanently unanswerable, and it should be struck rather than left looking pending.**\n\nComment #2 added: *\"does a section block's TEXT render in the in-channel `thread_broadcast` copy?\"* — the premise ADR 0020 Amendment 5 depended on and recorded as inferred rather than seen.\n\n⛔ **There is no in-channel copy any more.** Slack thread-broadcast is removed from oto entirely (git-bug `7570090`, owner ruling): `BroadcastPolicy`, `Warrants`, `ModeBroadcastReply`, `CapBroadcast`, `MsgOptionBroadcast()` and `broadcast_on_resolved` are all deleted, and ADR 0020 is superseded. So that question cannot be settled by any workspace visit, ever. **Struck, not deferred** — an observation nobody can make is worse than no entry, because it makes the checklist look incomplete when it is complete.\n\n⭐ **And the reason it went is worth recording here, because this ticket is the standing record of what oto has never seen work.** The broadcast set emptied itself rather than being argued away: four Reasons → two (Amendment 1) → `unacked_reminder` deleted (`bd0fb1d`) → `refired` producerless since ADR 0040 → `all_resolved` opt-in and default-off. On shipped defaults `Warrants` could already return true for **nothing at all**. So `reply_broadcast` joins the `@`-mention as a Slack parameter oto shipped, never observed working, and then removed — which is this ticket's whole thesis, twice over now.\n\n**The other four still stand and are unaffected**, since none of them involves broadcasting: `chat.update` of a root, a threaded reply, the resolved/snoozed card variants, and client parity.\n\n⚠️ **One is now MORE reachable than when it was written.** Comment #2 warned that observing any broadcast at all first required switching `broadcast_on_resolved` on, because nothing was reachable by default. That setup step is gone with the setting — everything left on this list is on the DEFAULT path, so a single connected workspace exercises all four without configuration.","files":null}]}